      {
        "id": "section_4",
        "narration": "Stop thinking of containers as mini virtual machines and start treating them as isolated, immutable process wrappers. They share your host kernel, leverage Namespaces for isolation, Cgroups for resource limits, and cached filesystem layers for lightning-fast deployments. <break time='0.6s'/> Master your Dockerfile layer order, respect kernel boundaries, and your build pipelines and production servers will run faster than ever.",
        "objective": "",
